  "gaps": [
    "The capture spans several programs (tail of a Supply Chain Management program whose heading is not captured, Computer Software Technology, and a truncated Cyber and Data Security Technology listing); this ledger covers only the Bachelor of Science in Computer Software Technology, the only program whose title and full requirement list are both captured.",
    "TEC 100 Computer Literacy replaces GEN 102 for this program, but the capture does not print TEC 100's credit value; 3 credits is assumed from the GEN 102 slot it replaces and the 33-credit Global Campus Foundations total and needs confirmation.",
    "ECO 203 (major) also satisfies 3 credits of Global Campus Foundations requirements, so the listed items sum to 123 against a 120-credit total; the capture does not state which Global Campus Foundations course or slot ECO 203 replaces.",
    "The capture says Global Campus Foundations courses 'may be substituted' but does not list the allowed substitutions or map courses to named requirement areas (e.g., Quantitative Reasoning, Natural Scientist Perspective referenced in prerequisites).",
    "GEN 101 (3 credits) is scheduled first and satisfies 3 elective credits, and GEN 104 (3 elective credits) is required for students transferring fewer than 30 credits; how these are counted within the 33-credit elective block is not itemized beyond that statement.",
    "Residency requirement of 30 credits at the University and 30 upper-division credits (18 in the major) apply, but the capture does not designate specific courses as institution-only; CST 499 must be taken last in the program."
  ],
